    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nFYI, updated neovim, and noticed that commit 3b88a8a65da17a49c6aad2d1bcb3eb2163577c06 breaks FS plugins such as `oil.nvim`.\nI am not sure whether it introduces functionalities long waited for that scope.\nBut, is this expected, i.e. this is a **breaking change** commit for some needed functionality?\nIf so, I guess it should be marked as such.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAs the commit is not marked with BREAKING CHANGES, it should maintain external functionality unchanged.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.13 commit 3b88a8a65da17a49c6aad2d1bcb3eb2163577c06\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux 22.04\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\n.\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\n.\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
